 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "57bc7b16-076a-5d7f-9700-faa7bbcaa22a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510296 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186509838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510296 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186509840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510296 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186509872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510296 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510296 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510296 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510296 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510296 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186510044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510296 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6a536d68-bf2d-5dad-99bc-e23331bfdfe7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510347 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186509696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510347 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186509708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510347 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186509723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510347 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186509751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510347 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510347 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510347 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510347 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186509696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510347 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d9278757-a57e-52ac-9515-43ca861ad9fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510376 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510376 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70492" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510376 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510376 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+4)^{2}+(z-2)^{2}=9$ and the line $x=y+1=\\frac{z-2}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510376 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2fc9ea0f-3211-5796-852b-f82127f7f8bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510376 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{1}=\\frac{y+1}{1}=\\frac{z-2}{2}=t\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=t \\\\ y &=t-1 \\\\ z &=2t+2,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y+4)^{2}+(z-2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (t)^{2}+((t-1)+4)^{2}+((2t+2)-2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (t)^{2}+(t+3)^{2}+(2t)^{2} & =9 \\\\ {t}^{2}+({t}^{2}+6t+9)+4{t}^{2} & =9 \\\\ 6{t}^{2}+6t+9 & =9 \\\\ 6{t}^{2}+6t & =0 \\\\ t(t+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=-1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=(0)=0 \\\\ y &=(0)-1=-1 \\\\ z &=2(0)+2=2,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(0,-1,2).$\n\n- For $t=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=(-1)=-1 \\\\ y &=(-1)-1=-2 \\\\ z &=2(-1)+2=0,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(-1,-2,0).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(0,-1,2)$ and $(-1,-2,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186510389 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510389 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35493" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510389 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510389 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{3}=-1$\nand the plane $3y+z=-2$  onto the\n$xy$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510389 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4aa33ace-7f3a-5239-9095-80fa2dcc03c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510389 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $z$, as follows:\n\n$$\n3y+z=-2\\,⟹\\,z=-2-3y\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the hyperboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{((-2-3y)+2)^{2}}{3} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{3} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2{y}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4{y}^{2} & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510479 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510479 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "07630e9e-6eaa-5c9c-8cca-3f82529d648d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510479 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510523 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8cafab22-633e-567a-b060-34f181932e1e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510523 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510542 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510542 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb05386a-05eb-5248-b754-a8d8d5a583d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510542 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510550 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510550 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e330baa0-4535-5227-ae2f-5e7087691796" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510550 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510565 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510565 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f9fa29ad-e929-5ec2-a636-229382ae0cca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510565 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186496282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547308 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186548082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547308 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186548090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547308 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186548112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547308 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186548132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547308 #edb/ref 1043 