edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547920 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547920 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547920 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547920 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547920 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547920 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547920 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547920 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186547702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547920 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a3b78ce5-61ca-5b12-8256-45eaecfa1b9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547920 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547984 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94941" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547984 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547984 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following best describes the projection of the intersection between the elliptic cone ${x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=2{z}^{2}$ and the plane $2z-x+1=0$ onto the $xy$-plane?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547984 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c9e9df7-050b-54af-a7dc-34ce03f716ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547984 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2z-x+1=0\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2} & =2{(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+3{y}^{2} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ {x}^{2}+3{y}^{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-x+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+x+3{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(x+1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}+3{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2}+3{y}^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipse centered at $(-1,0)$ in the $xy$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548041 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548041 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35267" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548041 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548041 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following best describes the projection of the intersection between the elliptic cone ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}={z}^{2}$ and the plane $2x-y=0$ onto the $xz$-plane?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548041 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aad779ca-b824-50cb-b4dc-f0dd2ba06356" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548041 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $y.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2x-y=0\\,⟹\\,y=2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $y$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(2x-1)^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}-4x+1 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2}-5{x}^{2}+4x & =1 \\\\ {z}^{2}-5({x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{5}x+\\frac{4}{25})+\\frac{4}{5} & =1 \\\\ {z}^{2}-5{({x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{5})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 5{z}^{2}-25{(x-\\frac{2}{5})}^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbola centered at $(\\frac{2}{5},0)$ in the $xz$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548082 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548082 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "00bf7e71-a2f6-5d03-9ce5-51e605b39bdf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548082 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548090 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548090 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1f2dfb02-7449-57f0-8474-7ab8cc23d410" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548090 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548112 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548170 #edb/ref 1759218604541